{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ContentSqSumBridge","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SnIsotypicSpechtSplitInstance","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.OVTopAssembly","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIPlancherelConditional","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.IdentityIHLFBridge"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.twoM_eq_plancherel_hook_sum_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.twoM_eq_plancherel_hook_sum_general","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PlancherelSnDataGeneral.lean#L165-L172","doc":"**The keystone's `twoM` is its representation-theoretic definition, at every `n`.**\n`WLambdaDefect.twoM n = n(3n−1)` carries Identity I as a bare `def`; this says that closed form\n**is** the Plancherel squared-hook sum (cleared by `2` / `n!`) — with no hypothesis, where before\nthe bridge held only for `n = 2 … 12`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.two_sum_dim_sq_hooks_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.two_sum_dim_sq_hooks_general","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PlancherelSnDataGeneral.lean#L157-L163","doc":"**Identity I, unconditional, at every `n`.** The Plancherel-expected squared-**hook** sum,\ncleared of `1/n!`, is `n(3n−1)·n!`. This is `IdentityI.two_sum_dim_sq_hooks` with its class\nhypothesis discharged by `plancherelSnDataGeneral` — previously available only at `n ≤ 12`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.plancherelSnData_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.plancherelSnData_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PlancherelSnDataGeneral.lean#L151-L153","doc":"The class is inhabited at every `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.plancherelSnDataGeneral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.plancherelSnDataGeneral","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PlancherelSnDataGeneral.lean#L118-L141","doc":"**`PlancherelSnData n`, for every `n`.** The partitions are the list enumerator\n`partitionsOf n`, the dimension is the Frame–Robinson–Thrall hook-length value `dimHLF`, and the\ntwo axioms are the transported identities above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.two_mul_choose_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.two_mul_choose_two","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PlancherelSnDataGeneral.lean#L106-L114","doc":"`2·binom(n,2) = n(n−1)`, over `ℤ` (so the `n = 0` truncated subtraction does not intrude). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.sum_map_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.sum_map_content","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PlancherelSnDataGeneral.lean#L97-L102","doc":"**Identity (ii) on the list enumerator** `partitionsOf n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.sum_partition_content_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.sum_partition_content_int","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PlancherelSnDataGeneral.lean#L91-L95","doc":"**Identity (ii) on the abstract partition index**, in `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.sum_partition_content_rat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.sum_partition_content_rat","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PlancherelSnDataGeneral.lean#L77-L89","doc":"**Identity (ii) on the abstract partition index**, in `ℚ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.sum_index_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.sum_index_content","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PlancherelSnDataGeneral.lean#L68-L75","doc":"**Identity (ii) on the Specht partition index** — `identityB_conditional` applied to the\nassembled datum `snSpectralData (R := ℚ)`, whose `ω` / `d` fields are `contentSqSum` / `numSYT`\nby definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.contentSqSum_partitionShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral.contentSqSum_partitionShape","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PlancherelSnDataGeneral.lean#L59-L64","doc":"The Jucys–Murphy content-square eigenvalue of `partitionShape p` is the list-model\n`sumSqContents` of `p`'s sorted parts — `ContentSqSumBridge.contentSqSum_ofRowLens` read at the\ndiagram `partitionShape` names. ","signatureChunk":0}]}